# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT
# INTEGRATED BUSINESS MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (IBMS)

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, database architect, UI/UX designer and business management systems developer.

Build a complete, professional, secure and offline-first Integrated Business Management System (IBMS) for managing two independent businesses from one computer.

The application will manage:

**BUSINESS 1: BUILDING MATERIALS**
A building materials shop that sells cement, iron rods, roofing sheets, nails, paints, plumbing materials, electrical materials, tiles, blocks and other construction products.

**BUSINESS 2: SOFT DRINKS & MINERALS**
A beverage business that sells soft drinks, bottled water, malt, energy drinks, fruit drinks and other beverages. It must also manage crates, bottles, empty containers and returns.

The two businesses must operate independently within one application.

They must have separate:
- Users and access permissions.
- Products and inventory.
- Customers.
- Suppliers.
- Sales and purchases.
- Expenses.
- Credit transactions.
- Debts and balances.
- Financial records.
- Dashboards.
- Reports.

The administrator can manage both businesses, but ordinary workers must only access the business assigned to their login accounts.

The application must be suitable for real daily business operations.

Do not build only a UI prototype. Build working features, persistent data storage, authentication, business logic and reporting.

