# 2. TECHNOLOGY AND APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE

Use a modern, maintainable full-stack architecture.

Preferred frontend:
- React.
- TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS.
- A professional component library where appropriate.
- Lucide icons.

Choose a reliable backend and database architecture that supports the requirements below.

### Local and offline-first operation

The application will initially be used on one shared computer by multiple users.

It must:
- Work without an internet connection after initial installation and setup.
- Save records persistently on the computer.
- Retain data after the application is closed or the computer restarts.
- Avoid requiring a continuous cloud connection.
- Support manual backup and restoration.
- Support exporting business records.
- Be installable on a Windows computer where the selected architecture permits.

Use a suitable persistent local database.

Preferred options:
- SQLite with a compatible local backend or desktop runtime.
- IndexedDB with Dexie if building a browser-based application.

Do not use temporary in-memory storage or browser session storage for business records.

If a browser-only architecture cannot reliably satisfy a requirement, explain the limitation and implement the most suitable alternative.

Do not falsely claim that the application works offline, uses SQLite or performs scheduled backups unless those capabilities have actually been implemented and tested.

### Application structure

Use modular architecture so that each business module can be developed and maintained independently.

Keep shared functionality such as authentication, user management, audit logs and backup management in the application foundation.

All business records must have proper ownership and access controls.

